        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Option<P> Scene impl doesn't forward register_dependencies",
        "explanation": "The tuple Scene impl forwards both resolve and register_dependencies to inner scenes. This impl only overrides resolve, so Option<P> uses the trait's default register_dependencies, which presumably does nothing (the impl compiles without the method, so a default exists). If the wrapped scene depends on an asset (e.g. it inherits from a .bsn asset), the dependency is never registered. queue_spawn_scene then won't wait for it, and resolve can fail with ResolveSceneError::MissingSceneDependency.",
        "suggestion": "Add `fn register_dependencies(&self, dependencies: &mut SceneDependencies) { if let Some(scene) = self { scene.register_dependencies(dependencies); } }`.",
        "evidence": "impl<P> Scene for Option<P>",
        "confidence": 0.75,
